From: PonWrt
Subject: [PATCH] oam: report the CTC ONU SN layout again

Upstream 10f4a9e and a903fcc replaced the ONU SN attribute (branch 0xC7,
leaf 0x0001) with the 8-byte ONU serial number, which was tested against
one Huawei OLT. The CTC layout is vendor ID (4), ONU model (4), ONU ID
(the MAC address, 6), hardware version (8) and software version (16),
plus the extended ONU model (16) from CTC 3.0 on, as before.

On a China Telecom 10G-EPON line, a FiberHome HG5585F CT registers with
the seller's firmware, whose agent predates 10f4a9e and so sends the CTC
layout. With the 8-byte version the same unit registers and is then
deregistered and denied, as is a Nokia XG-040G-TF. The ONU SN is the
likeliest difference; this is not confirmed yet.

- Report the CTC layout again. `option onu_sn_format 'serial'` in the
  oam section keeps the 8-byte serial number for OLTs that want it.
- An unset vendor ID follows the vendor bytes of the serial number the
  line registers with, instead of OWRT. A configured one still wins.
- Read the active serial number for every OAMPDU instead of once at
  start: the driver latches it when pon0 opens, which is after this agent
  starts (START=19, network at 20), so the first read is usually "none"
  and the ONU SN then carried OWRT and part of the MAC address. A change
  is logged as an "identity" event.
---
